Package: NationalModelUng2009
Title: National Stand-Volume Models for Canadian Tree Species (Ung et al. 2009)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Derek Felix", "Sattler", email = "derek.sattler@nrcan-rncan.gc.ca", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("His Majesty the King in Right of Canada, as represented by the Minister of Natural Resources", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Implements the two national growth-and-yield models of Ung, Bernier,
    Guo and Lambert (2009) <doi:10.5558/tfc85057-1>. Given stand age, annual
    degree-days above 0 C and mean annual precipitation, 'Nat1' predicts dominant
    height, basal area and gross merchantable volume, and 'Nat2' predicts volume
    directly, for 25 Canadian commercial tree species. The package validates
    inputs, warns when a prediction falls outside the data the models were fitted
    to or is very sensitive to the climate inputs, and can look up climate
    values with the 'climr' package.
